WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.550
The reference leaves a short
list of decisions to the agency.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.347
Which narrow classes, if any,

3
00:00:05.347 --> 00:00:09.175
the authorizing official
accepts for autonomous closure.

4
00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.512
Who actually holds the escalation roles.

5
00:00:11.512 --> 00:00:14.437
How classes map to lanes
in your own record.

6
00:00:14.437 --> 00:00:16.988
What targets you set
for the five measures.

7
00:00:16.988 --> 00:00:19.638
And an end date for
every declared exception.

8
00:00:19.638 --> 00:00:23.443
For the full argument, read
Chapter 10, then the drift engine,

9
00:00:23.443 --> 00:00:27.249
the evidence chapter and the
control mapping in Appendix A.

10
00:00:27.249 --> 00:00:28.350
Thanks for watching.

11
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.146
Remember: a ticket is
evidence only when it

12
00:00:31.146 --> 00:00:34.730
authorized something that
ran, and a re-read proved it.
